<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THOR's pointer service.

  It observes nothing. `accessibilityEventTypes` is empty and the feedback type is
  generic because this service is not reading the screen — it exists solely to
  receive controller buttons while another app has focus, draw a cursor over that
  app, and dispatch the taps the cursor makes. Requesting event types it does not
  use would mean being woken for every window change on the device.

  `canRequestFilterKeyEvents` plus `flagRequestFilterKeyEvents` is what allows
  `onKeyEvent` to see buttons at all, and to consume them so a click does not also
  reach the game underneath.

  `canPerformGestures` is what allows `dispatchGesture`, which is the only way an
  unprivileged app can click inside another one.

  `canRetrieveWindowContent` is what allows the on-screen keyboard to type into
  another app, and it is the one capability here that is genuinely invasive: it
  is permission to read the contents of every window, not only the field being
  filled in. Android has a narrower slot for this — an input method — and that
  would have been the better trade. This is the route taken instead, so the
  description shown at the moment of granting says plainly what it allows.

  Used for exactly two calls: `findFocus(FOCUS_INPUT)` to locate the field the
  user has tapped, and `ACTION_SET_TEXT` to fill it in. Nothing is stored, and
  no window is inspected unless a key has just been pressed on Loki's keyboard.

  `canTakeScreenshot` is what allows a screenshot of a game, which is another
  app on another display and therefore something the launcher cannot capture on
  its own. The alternative is `MediaProjection`, which asks the system's consent
  dialog every time — on top of the very thing being photographed. Used only when
  the user presses the screenshot action; nothing is captured on a timer, on an
  event, or in the background, and every frame is written into the active
  profile's own directory and nowhere else.
-->
<accessibility-service
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeWindowStateChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackGeneric"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagRequestFilterKeyEvents|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:canPerformGestures="true"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canTakeScreenshot="true"
    android:canRequestFilterKeyEvents="true"
    android:description="@string/mouse_service_description"
    android:notificationTimeout="0"
    android:summary="@string/mouse_service_summary" />
